target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheDecodeErrorNamesWhatTheOperatorMustGoFix'
expect: the fields are not in a fixed order
why:    Go map iteration order is random, so without the sort the same corrupt row prints a different message on every run — which makes an operator-facing message unquotable in a bug report and an `expect:` string unpinnable. Survived the suite until this case existed, because every fixture carried exactly one misplaced field.
--- old
	sort.Strings(bad) // map order is random; an error message must not be
--- new
